title: The Ha Giang Loop — what four days really cost (2026)
format: story
charstyle: nutshell
voice: af_heart
music: adventure
score: adventure@1 night@2 upbeat@3 tension@4 adventure@5 night@6 wonder@7 emotional@8 upbeat@9
sources: Vietadvisor "Ha Giang Loop Cost" receipt, Sep 2026 (sleeper cabin 350k each way; XR150 450k/day; semi-auto ~200k/day; border permit 230k; fuel ~11 L 250k; homestays 300–350k; dinner 100–150k; food & drinks 1.17M; Lung Cu 25k + 10k parking; Nho Que boat 150k; total 5,285,000 VND ≈ $203; damage fees $50–300; 3M VND cash; ATMs Ha Giang city, Dong Van, Meo Vac; easy rider tip $10–20/day); Tuoi Tre News 15 Apr 2026 (350 km loop; tightened rules for licensed operators); vietnamtourism.com "Ha Giang Loop — the honest 2026 guide" (homestays 300–500k; riding without a valid licence: fine 4–5M VND; zero-alcohol breath tests; fog under 10 m Nov–Feb); zinghomehagiang.com permit guide (230–300k). Checked Oct 2026.
// ANGLE   Everyone asks "how much is the Ha Giang Loop?" — Dave counts every dong of four days, live, and the total lands $3 over.
// HERO    Dave wants the loop for under $200. BUT a checkpoint; THEREFORE the licence; BUT corn wine; THEREFORE tea; BUT fog;
//         THEREFORE slow — and the receipt on the night bus home.
// LOOK    illustrated karst mountains (3 parallax layers + haze), a road that scrolls under the bike, terraces, a sleeper bus at
//         night, a rental shop, a checkpoint, a clay homestay, Ma Pi Leng canyon. A running receipt clipped top-left counts up.
// COLOUR  bright day → night bus blue → dawn town → noon road → warm night homestay → misty canyon → bus-night gold → day → lantern dusk.
// SOUND   engine revs, bus brake, shutter clicks, stamp, skid at the checkpoint, fuel glug, crickets + bowls at dinner, wind + fog.
// VIRAL   odometer cold open + "under $200?" in 2 s; a counter viewers compete with (guess the total); a twist ($3 over);
//         save card acted out; open loop to Hoi An.

// 0:00 ECU: an odometer rolls 000 → 350 with the needle swinging, WHIP OUT: Dave rides a mountain road, karst peaks scrolling,
//      "DAVE" tag, "UNDER $200?" slams, a tape runs 350 KM across the valley, an easy rider passes the other way.
# vis kind=hg act=hook
This is Dave. Dave wants to ride the Ha Giang Loop for under two hundred dollars.
Three hundred and fifty kilometres. Four days.
Let's count every dong.
// 0:12 ZOOM THROUGH the headlight into night: a sleeper bus rolls past moonlit karst; Dave asleep in a lit cabin (Zzz); the
//      receipt ticks +350,000; the bus brakes, "4:00 AM" drops in; the driver says stay till eight.
# vis kind=hg act=bus spent=350000 adds="350000@0" trans=zoomthru tc=.6,.62
It starts with the night bus from Hanoi. A sleeper cabin: three hundred and fifty thousand.
It rolls in at four in the morning.
Some companies let you sleep on board until eight.
// 0:24 BLOOM into dawn: a rental shop in Ha Giang city, two bikes with price boards; Dave weighs them, picks the XR150 (+1.8M),
//      snaps every scratch (SNAP! SNAP!), the owner stamps his passport for the permit (+230K).
# vis kind=hg act=rent spent=2380000 adds="1800000@2|230000@4" trans=bloom tc=.5,.3 tcol=#ffd98a
In Ha Giang city, an XR150 rents for four hundred and fifty thousand a day.
A semi-automatic is about two hundred. No clutch is easier on these passes.
Dave rides a manual at home, so: XR150. Four days, one point eight million.
Photograph every scratch. Damage fees run fifty to three hundred dollars.
The border permit: two hundred and thirty thousand, with your passport.
// 0:50 WHIP to a checkpoint: Dave skids to a stop, an officer raises a hand; Dave pats every pocket, sweating; "FINE: MILLIONS"
//      slams; he finds his licence, "PHEW!", the barrier lifts.
# vis kind=hg act=check spent=2380000 trans=whip
But at the first checkpoint, the officer wants one thing.
A licence Vietnam recognises.
Without one: a fine of millions, and your insurance won't pay.
Dave has his. Phew.
// 1:03 SLICES onto the open road: hairpins below, "DAY 1" drops, a tape runs 100 KM; a roadside pump slides in, GLUG GLUG (+250K).
# vis kind=hg act=ride spent=2630000 adds="250000@1" trans=slices
Day one: about a hundred kilometres to Yen Minh.
Fuel for the whole loop: around eleven litres. Two hundred and fifty thousand.
// 1:11 BLOBS into night: a clay homestay, the family serves dinner (+950K for three nights); grandpa lifts the corn wine,
//      "LIMIT: 0" drops, Dave asks for tea and everybody laughs.
# vis kind=hg act=stay spent=3580000 adds="950000@0" trans=blobs
Nights are homestays, three hundred to three hundred and fifty thousand.
Dinner with the family: one hundred to one hundred and fifty.
Corn wine is free. But for riders, the limit is zero.
So Dave smiles, says thank you, and sticks to tea.
// 1:27 MATCH the steam into morning cloud: Ma Pi Leng, the road on the cliff, the Nho Que far below with a tiny boat (+150K);
//      fog rolls in, a tape shows 10 M, Dave slows, headlight on.
# vis kind=hg act=pass spent=3730000 adds="150000@1" trans=match tc=.5,.55 tc2=.5,.4
Day three: Ma Pi Leng, high above the Nho Que river.
The boat down there costs one hundred and fifty thousand.
Fog can cut visibility to ten metres in minutes. Ride slow.
// 1:39 ZOOM THROUGH the fog into a bus window at night: Dave unrolls a receipt that keeps going; food, coffee and a flag tower
//      ticket land (+1.55M with the bus home); "5,285,000 VND" drops, "$203" slams, "+$3", Dave laughs.
# vis kind=hg act=sum spent=5285000 adds="1555000@0" trans=zoomthru tc=.5,.5
Back on the night bus home, Dave adds up the rest: food, coffee, a flag tower ticket.
The total: five million, two hundred and eighty-five thousand dong.
About two hundred and three dollars. Three over… worth it.
// 1:52 WHIP to a roadside: Dave counts cash (3M VND), a signpost pops three ATM boards, an easy rider pulls up, "TIP $10–20 / DAY".
# vis kind=hg act=rules spent=5285000 trans=whip last="TIP $10–20 / DAY"
Save this: bring three million dong in cash.
ATMs are only in Ha Giang city, Dong Van and Meo Vac.
No licence? Book an easy rider, and tip ten to twenty dollars a day.
// 2:05 ZOOM THROUGH a lantern: Hoi An river at dusk, floating lanterns, Dave on a little boat — "NEXT: HOI AN".
# vis kind=hg act=tease trans=zoomthru tc=.5,.45
Next time, Dave heads south… to Hoi An.
